# std/DOMAINS — The 8 Functional Domains

File: std/docs/DOMAINS.oot

This file describes each of the 8 functional domains in the
openOODA standard library. For every domain we list: scope,
sub-hubs, and one or two example .oo modules.

A domain is a self-contained subtree under std/. Each one ships its
own ANCHOR.oo at the root. Import that ANCHOR.oo to pull in the full
public surface for that domain.

## 1. core/ — universal primitives

Scope: the foundation layer. Every other domain imports from core/.
Nothing in core/ imports from any other domain.

  Sub-hubs:
    primitives/   Option, Result, List, Str, byte, ast, macro, semver
    math/         stats, bigint, complex, matrix, polynomial, fraction
    text/         regex, KMP, Levenshtein, UTF-8, diff, rope
    encoding/     hex, base64/32/58, varint, msgpack, cbor, bencode
    collection/   Vec, Queue, HashMap, HashSet, List, BitSet, Trie
    io/           Reader, Writer, Cursor, Buffered, Pipe, BitReader
    format/       print, parse, verify, config, normalize
    markup/       JSON, XML, YAML, TOML, Protobuf wire
    cli/          CliCommand, parser, completion, prompts, style
    principles/   CODATA 2022 constants, units, zero-ambient cap
    proofs/       formal_proofs and proof_verifiers

  Examples:
    std/core/primitives/option.oo
    std/core/math/algebraic.oo

## 2. fs/ — filesystem, OS, time, archive

Scope: the disk, the operating system, the clock, and the byte
streams that move through them. Pure compute lives in core/.

  Sub-hubs:
    file/         Path, FileInfo, FileReader/Writer, Glob, Watch, Jail
    os/           terminal, cpu, gpu, microvm, cgroups, eBPF, scheduler
    process/      cmd, env, process, signal, rlimit, python
    time/         chrono (durations, instants, calendars, monotonic)
    archive/      archive, gzip, tar, zip, zstd, pcap reader
    compression/  huffman, lz4, lz77, brotli, neural image

  Examples:
    std/fs/file/dir_entry.oo
    std/fs/compression/huffman.oo

## 3. net/ — network, transport, sync, actor

Scope: anything that crosses a process or machine boundary, plus
the concurrency primitives that orchestrate it.

  Sub-hubs:
    protocol/     wire, app protocols, http, http2, http3, quic
    transport/    telecom, 5G, 6G
    mesh/         p2p, edge
    telemetry/    packet capture, ids, dpi
    sync/         concurrency primitives (was std/sync)
    actor/        actor model (was std/actor)

  Examples:
    std/net/protocol/http_client.oo
    std/net/sync/mutex.oo (illustrative; check current surface)

## 4. sec/ — security

Scope: the security surface. Cryptography, capability, attestation,
TEE, threat modeling, fuzz, redteam, policy.

  Sub-hubs:
    hash/         blake2, blake3, sha2, sha3, adler32
    symmetric/    aes, chacha20
    asymmetric/   rsa, ed25519, x25519
    mac/          hmac, poly1305
    zk/           zero-knowledge proofs
    enclave/      SGX, SEV-SNP, TDX, TrustZone
    capability/   object capabilities, rights masks, dim/unforge
    control/      access control engines
    exploit/      catalog and verification of known weakness classes
    ct/           constant-time primitives
    ai/           model and prompt security
    net/          net-facing policy
    cps/          cyber-physical security
    defense/      intrusion detection, hardening
    rasp/         runtime application self-protection
    string_encrypt/  string-level encryption helpers
    sys/          OS-level security helpers
    laws/         security laws and theories (private siblings)

  Examples:
    std/sec/hash/blake3_codec.oo
    std/sec/capability/capability.oo

## 5. science/ — physics, chem, bio, econ, comm

Scope: the natural and social sciences that the rest of the system
relies on. Laws, theories, and computations, not data.

  Sub-hubs:
    phys/         mechanics, EM, optics, thermodyne, relativity, gnc
    chem/         reactions, periodic trends, spectra
    bio/          genetics, neuroscience, ecology, immunology
    econ/         markets, finance, fintech, DeFi
    comm/         satellite (DVB-S2/S2X, GNSS, ISL)

  Examples:
    std/science/phys/newton.oo (illustrative)
    std/science/econ/black_scholes.oo (illustrative)

## 6. app/ — applied software

Scope: the user-facing applications. AI, robotics, UI, data,
agents, combat.

  Sub-hubs:
    ai/           tensors, transformer, quant, GGUF, scaling law
    robot/        robotics, ros2, mpc, lidar, iiot, digital_twin
    ui/           3d, gui, tui, wui, game_engine, media, codecs
    data/         db, dataframe, columnar, graph, vector_ann, cloud
    agent/        synthesizer, repair, evolution, pair_programmer, repl
    combat/       military combat, missiles, formation, air combat

  Examples:
    std/app/ai/tensor.oo (illustrative)
    std/app/data/connection.oo (illustrative)

## 7. hw/ — hardware theory

Scope: the laws, theories, and principles of computer architecture.
This domain is a theoretical-foundation library. It exposes no
public API code. The directory is documentation and verification
rules, used by audit harnesses and hardware-correctness proofs.

  Sub-hubs:
    silicon/      aarch64, riscv, x86 ABI, alu, bind, bool
    gpu/          GPU architectures and the bandwidth model
    mem/          memory subsystem theory
    bare_metal/   bare-metal boot and runtime theory
    runtime/      runtime / kernel boundary theory
    drivers_hal/  driver and HAL theory

  Top-level files (no sub-hub):
    amdahls_law_hw.oo, branch_predictor_principle.oo,
    cache_associativity_law.oo, cache_line_law.oo,
    cxl_3_0_law.oo, dram_refresh_theory.oo,
    endianness_law.oo, memory_bandwidth_law.oo,
    moesi_protocol_theory.oo, page_offset_law.oo,
    tage_predictor_principle.oo, twos_complement_law.oo

  Example:
    std/hw/amdahls_law_hw.oo
    std/hw/silicon/aarch64_abi.oo

## 8. meta/ — test and diagnostic infrastructure

Scope: the scaffolding used to verify the other 7 domains. Test
harnesses, fuzzers, mutation, diagnostic types, log levels, metrics,
telemetry, tracer.

  Sub-hubs:
    test/         fuzz, fault_injection, multi_compiler, mutation,
                  GPU cross-validation, scenario, runner
    diag/         backtrace, breadcrumb, event_timeline, health,
                  invariant eval, log levels, metrics, panic hook,
                  stopwatch, telemetry, tracer

  Examples:
    std/meta/test/fault_injection.oo
    std/meta/diag/event_timeline.oo (illustrative)
